<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><atom:link href="https://merithumanist.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><title>The Meritocratic Humanist</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/</link><description>Humanism. Merit. Consequence. A continuing log on earned excellence.</description><language>en</language><item><title>Log 060: Rupture</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/060/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/060/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:03:01 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/060/image.png&quot; alt=&quot;The Amalgaverse title card: the word AMALGAVERSE in white text over a starfield and galaxy.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fractions formed, factions arose, exclusion resulted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;IPs in ruin, promising returns killed at the 11th hour.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Studios haemorrhage, creators unsatisfied, audiences won&#x27;t wait.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What&#x27;s left; potential, &quot;There are always possibilities&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 059: The IP</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/059/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/059/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:00:01 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/059/image.png&quot; alt=&quot;Screenshot of an X thread. The Meritocratic Humanist: &amp;quot;If you have moved on, after multiple failed Stargate continuations, who would blame you. For many, the last Stargate episode shall be the final one with your name in the credits. Thank you.&amp;quot; Brad Wright replies: &amp;quot;Actually, I had already moved on when they called me the first time in 2017, when they asked me to do another “Origins”. I was busy making Travelers, and they had no budget. Then, in 2019, they asked me to create a new series, but that show died with the pandemic and MGM&amp;#x27;s sale to Amazon. When they hired Martin to create a new Stargate he asked me to consult, and of course, because it was Martin, I agreed. Then they killed it too after he&amp;#x27;d worked on it for two years. So yeah. I have moved on.&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The brand name is meaningless.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The value of any art, is in the desire of the audience for the creator&#x27;s creation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Discarding the creators who breathed life into the art also discards the audience that made the IP valuable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 058: Grace</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/058/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/058/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:04:39 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/058/image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;A child places a stone atop a cairn of balanced stones on a pebble beach.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Obligations to our commitments, even when it&#x27;s hardest, help define who we are.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibility and Dignity carry us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Face Death the same as Life. The relationship is not over: redefined.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 057: The Flag</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/057/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/057/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 13:03:15 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/057/image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;The empty captain&amp;#x27;s chair from the original series.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sci-Fi examines morals or aspects of culture by turning the screw.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trek made a declaration about us, then turned the screw.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modern Trek skips the declaration, then turns the screw in the opposite direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Declaration matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 056: The Audience</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/056/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/056/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 13:03:47 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/056/image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;The Hollywood sign, circa 1970s. Several letters have collapsed or fallen; the structure is weathered and sagging on the hillside.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Effort, craft and honesty creates media worth time and investment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Branding negative reaction as the reason for underperformance alienates the ones who justify the media&#x27;s existence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Take ownership for the failures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 055: Vigil</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/055/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/055/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:03:42 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/055/image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;The refit USS Enterprise orbiting a planet lit by dawn.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As this era of Star Trek closes the future is uncertain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prequels and Reboots serve the creator, not the audience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Creativity, Competence and the Unknown.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Audiences have waited for over 30 years, and still wait...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Special Log 002: The Threshold</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/SL002/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/SL002/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 13:02:24 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/SL002/image.png&quot; alt=&quot;A schematic of a sextant overlaid on the Star Trek delta, the emblem of The Meritocratic Humanist.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Undiscovered Country&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 054: Spectrum of Humanity</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/054/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/054/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 13:02:51 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&quot;Modern society&#x27;s&quot; obsession with sorting by sexuality and identity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The label becomes a membership of a club; a caste.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Human individuality replaced by the definition of the label.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 053: 1987-2011</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/053/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/053/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 23:00:57 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/053/image-1.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Marty gestures across the briefing table in Stargate SG-1&amp;#x27;s &amp;quot;200&amp;quot;. Subtitle: &amp;quot;Never underestimate your audience.&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/053/image-2.png&quot; alt=&quot;Mitchell, Vala and Carter listen at the briefing table. Subtitle: &amp;quot;They&amp;#x27;re generally sensitive, intelligent people&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/053/image-3.png&quot; alt=&quot;The same table, Carter now smiling. Subtitle: &amp;quot;who respond positively to quality entertainment.&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Respect for the audience began with writing compelling characters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The lessons learnt in 2012 from $1.5b, resulted in discarding what made those Halcyon days, Golden.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The audience was always there, and still is, waiting…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 052: Dignity</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/052/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/052/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 23:00:22 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/052/image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Maximus&amp;#x27; hand brushing the tops of a wheat field as he enters Elysium, in Gladiator.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Relationships, Convictions and Actions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grief carries us through loss; we either learn to live with it, or we don&#x27;t.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Is there Something for you to Believe In?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 051: Weaponisation</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/051/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/051/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 11:31:02 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/051/image.jpeg&quot; alt=&quot;PinkNews quote graphic of Russell T Davies, smiling, in a dark jacket and green shirt. Quote: &amp;quot;All our lives we&amp;#x27;ve campaigned to be more visible. Now I look at myself like I&amp;#x27;m an idiot. As if I ever imagined we&amp;#x27;d reach a harmonious society. Our visibility is being weaponised.&amp;quot; Caption: Russell T Davies on the current issues with LGBTQ+ visibility.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Representation reduces: the actor to a label, the character to a position, the work to a sermon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&quot;Visibility&quot; used to the exclusion of all others, excludes and weaponises the cause.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 050: The Price</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/050/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/050/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 23:00:38 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;Corporate apathy, creator apathy, audience apathy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Culture, a Monument, once built to feed all 3, discarded its  &quot;Legacy&quot;, the cost isn&#x27;t the apathy: the loss of the Symbiosis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 049: The &quot;Legacy&quot; Fan</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/049/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/049/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 04 Jun 2026 23:00:27 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/049/image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;The active Stargate at the top of the ramp in the gate room, its blue event horizon shimmering.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 60s, 70s, 80s and 90s captivated the imagination in audiences of all ages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Their shows were accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Intention to pursue new and young audiences; accessible to no one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 048: Representation of Culture</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/048/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/048/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 25 May 2026 23:00:52 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/048/image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;The Friends title card: the orange sofa lit by a lamp beside a fountain, against a dark city skyline.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Movie about Ancient Greece, without representation of the Culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Show about 6 friends in &#x27;90s New York, representing white friends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Representation of the depicted culture or representation of the projected culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 047: Crisis of Competence Pt III</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/047/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/047/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 21 May 2026 23:00:53 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/047/image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Data seated at the hearing table, his hand resting on a panel, in &amp;quot;The Measure of a Man&amp;quot;.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Structured Thought interpreted in different ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Humanity sees Artificial Intelligence.&lt;br&gt;
Artificial Intelligence sees Humanity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Different ways of interpreting Structured Thought.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 046: Uni-Partisan</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/046/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/046/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 18 May 2026 23:00:46 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/046/image.png&quot; alt=&quot;An antique brass sextant on a wooden desk, with the Log&amp;#x27;s text overlaid: &amp;quot;Not my President&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Stolen Election&amp;quot;. Radical and Reasonable. Inclusive and Exclusive. Opposing Ideologies. Same structure. Same effect. Same result.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Not my President&quot; and &quot;Stolen Election&quot;.&lt;br&gt;
Radical and Reasonable.&lt;br&gt;
Inclusive and Exclusive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Opposing Ideologies. Same structure. Same effect. Same result.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 045: Divergence</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/045/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/045/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 14 May 2026 23:19:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/045/image.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Starfleet Academy cadets walking together, laughing, through a gleaming corridor.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Through Tris Prior the world was shown the dangers of the Caste.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But instead we were told to embrace factions by recognising labels such as &quot;Strong Female Lead&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 044: Break the Walls Down</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/044/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/044/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 07 May 2026 22:49:56 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/044/image.png&quot; alt=&quot;Illustration of a snake built from a stone wall, uncoiling, with rays of light passing through its gaps. Text: &amp;quot;Meet the argument, see the person, draw the conclusion on merit. The Snake unfolds.&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Meet the argument, see the person, draw the conclusion on merit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Snake unfolds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 043: Our Rob or Ross</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/043/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/043/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 07 May 2026 22:44:14 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/043/image.png&quot; alt=&quot;Illustration of an ouroboros, a snake biting its own tail, its body cracking with light. Text: &amp;quot;Labelling discourse &amp;#x27;Toxic&amp;#x27; to shutdown discourse is in itself... Toxic. Forcing the label onto the person creates the mirror. The snake folds back on itself.&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Labelling discourse &quot;Toxic&quot; to shutdown discourse is in itself... Toxic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forcing the label onto the person creates the mirror.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Snake Folds back on itself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Log 042: Legacies</title><link>https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/042/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/042/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 07 Apr 2026 11:46:02 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/042/image-1.webp&quot; alt=&quot;Men watch ships at the mouth of the Strait of Hormuz from Khor Fakkan at dusk. Text: &amp;quot;What we do now,&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://merithumanist.github.io/logs/042/image-2.webp&quot; alt=&quot;Aerial view of the Colosseum, Rome. Text: &amp;quot;echoes in eternity.&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;What we do now, echoes in eternity.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#TheMeritocraticHumanist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>
